A **buyer's market** has **supply above demand**, so prices fall; a seller's market is the reverse. Perishable vegetables need a **very short-period market**. When total product is constant, **marginal product is zero**. **Shadow prices** for public projects came from **Jan Tinbergen**. The **P/V (profit-volume) ratio** improves by raising prices, changing the sales mix or cutting variable cost.

@up UP link: The most widely held insurance in UP's villages comes from **PM Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana** (life) and **PM Suraksha Bima Yojana** (accident), both from **2015** and sold through bank and post office accounts.

@trap
**LIC 1956 → UTI Feb 1964 → IDBI July 1964 → SEBI 1988/1992.** **IRDAI regulates insurance (Hyderabad).** **No indemnity in life insurance.** **SEBI regulates mutual funds; private MFs from 1993.** **Sensex 30, Greenex 25; Nikkei = Tokyo.** **Broker is not a speculator.** **Gilt-edged = government securities.** **Commercial paper = corporates.** **CRISIL 1987 → ICRA 1991 → CARE 1993.** **Buyer's market = supply > demand.** **MRP = maximum, can bargain below.** **Shadow prices: Tinbergen.**
@end

